<rml>
<head>
	<title>Pause menu</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="pauseMenu.rcss"/>
</head>
<!-- The pause menu. The engine shows this document and binds the data model "pause_menu" (see src/systems/menu.h):
       settings.<name>   the value of an option (a slider can be data-value="settings.masterVolume")
       labels.<name>     its text: "MSAA 4x", "75%", "On"
       enabled.<name>    whether it matters now (the FSR sharpness only while FSR is on)
       screen            "main" or any name you give to a div with data-if="screen == 'name'"
     and the events set('name', value), step('name', 1), toggle('name'), show('screen'), back(), resume(), quit(),
     open('ui/other.rml') (another menu over this one: Options is options.rml, shared with the main menu) and
     action('name'), which calls onMenuAction("pause", name) in the game script. This file
     is yours: change the screens, the texts and pauseMenu.rcss as you like. -->
<body data-model="pause_menu">
	<div class="card" data-if="screen == 'main'">
		<div class="title">Paused</div>
		<button data-event-click="resume()">Resume</button>
		<button data-event-click="open('ui/options.rml')">Options</button>
		<button class="quit" data-event-click="quit()">Quit</button>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
